sweet-sampler-deep (lowclk 2026-11-14): the process sampler (0054/0055) reaches deeper, prints short rows and takes its pace from two boot-args.
Why [read docs/research/153-coreduetd-biome-runaway.md]: the caller of coreduetd's endless _DKBiomeQuery is unknown; the SMP backtrace row was cut by the USB log line
limit (about 358 characters) and the walk (16 frames) did not reach above `_DKKnowledgeStorage _executeQuery:error:`; the sampler also ran only every 120 s.
Changed (read-only: no register, no hardware access, no new write): (1) boot-args sweetsampleiv=N (seconds between samples, decimal 5..600, default 120) and
sweetsamplemax=N (samples, decimal 1..60, default 40 = what 0055 left; the brief's "10" is the 0054 value). Read as strings (PE_parse_boot_arg_str with literal names, not PE_parse_boot_argn
into a char[]); empty, hex, signed, trailing text or out of range logs `SWEET GAP: sweetsample...` and keeps the default. The first sample stays at 90 s.
(2) the frame walk goes up to SWEET_SMP_BT_MAX = 48 frames (osfmk/kern/exception.c, was 16). Guards of 0054 kept (fp non-zero, 8-aligned, readable through
vm_map_read_user, next fp above this one); added: fp must be below vm_map_max(map). NOT added: a per-thread stack range, no cited source for it in this tree.
(3) rows: first row unchanged in format "SMP name tN pc 0x.. lr 0x.. sp 0x.. bt 0x.. ...", further frames in "SMP name tN bt[k] 0x.. ..." rows, k = 0-based index of the
first frame on the row; at most 8 addresses per row and every row shorter than 200 characters (SMP_ROW_LIM). The header row (slide, mh) is untouched.
With neither boot-arg the output equals today's except: the first row ends where the 200 character bound is reached instead of holding up to 16 frames, the rest
follows in bt[k] rows, and walks can be deeper than 16 frames. Documented in the header of sweet_sample.c.
Host test: tools/test_sweet_sample_core.py compiles the SMP_CORE block (parse + row split). The kernel glue is not run there.
ORDER: after 0055 (and 0054).
